T1100: start the WMT core from wmt_detect without a userspace launcher

The vendor stack expects a userspace launcher to open /dev/stpwmt and issue
COMBO_IOCTL_DO_MODULE_INIT, which is the only caller of
mtk_wcn_common_drv_init() -> WMT_init().  This port runs no launcher, so
WMT_init() never ran and the t1100_btif_stp bring-up (STP over BTIF,
CONNSYS power on, ROMv4 patch download) was never scheduled.

Call mtk_wcn_common_drv_init() at the end of wmt_detect_driver_init() when
t1100_btif_stp is set.  With the parameter unset the old behaviour (wlan_drv
powers the chip on) is preserved.

--- a/common_detect/wmt_detect.c
+++ b/common_detect/wmt_detect.c
@@ -348,6 +348,19 @@
 
 	WMT_DETECT_PR_INFO("driver(major %d) installed success\n", gWmtDetectMajor);
 
+	/* T1100: the port runs no userspace launcher to issue
+	 * COMBO_IOCTL_DO_MODULE_INIT, so start the WMT core right here.  With
+	 * t1100_btif_stp set it selects STP over BTIF and powers CONNSYS on,
+	 * which downloads the ROMv4 patches (see WMT_init()). */
+	{
+		extern int t1100_btif_stp;
+		extern int mtk_wcn_common_drv_init(void);
+
+		if (t1100_btif_stp)
+			WMT_DETECT_PR_INFO("t1100: mtk_wcn_common_drv_init() -> %d\n",
+					   mtk_wcn_common_drv_init());
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 
